    array.push(cH, "Another day, another push for the dollar, while the euro waits for fresh French clues.|The pound passed its growth test, but it didn't win the day.|A Bank of Japan dove spoke up, and the yen's December hopes got a little quieter.|The franc stayed silent again, and the dollar kept the floor.|Oil stayed soft, and the widest gap on our board stayed wide.|A quiet day in Australia left the dollar doing all the talking.|The kiwi had another empty page, and the Fed kept writing.|The pound took its test and passed it quietly, so the stand-off goes on.|Today's BoJ news pulled the yen's strongest scenario further away.|No new French data and no Swiss news: the thin lean stays thin.|The knife-edge pair is still balancing, with no new push from either side.|Two quiet currencies, one more day without a winner.|Oil softened again, and the slim euro lean stayed on its feet.|Sterling's growth number came in as expected, and a BoJ dove trimmed the yen's upside scenario.|The pound cleared its hurdle without drama, so the lean stays thin.|The UK's growth report landed on target, and the Aussie kept its narrow edge.|The pound had its turn, and the stand-off survived it.|Oil drifted lower again while the pound got an on-target growth report.|A dovish voice in Tokyo made the bearish scenario for this pair less likely.|Another day without a tie-breaker.|Two quiet neighbours, and the Aussie keeps its thin lead.|Oil's soft start on Thursday kept the commodity cousins apart.|The kiwi stayed quiet, and Tokyo's message turned mixed.|Neither side spoke today, so the thin lean is unchanged.|Oil's slide kept the kiwi's thin lead in place.|Oil weaker and a BoJ dove: the lean holds, the extreme scenario fades.|Weaker oil, a silent franc: the lean holds.|Two safe havens, and tonight the yen's case got a little softer.|Gold's slide continued, and its main enemy, higher rates, is still in the room.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED (strengthened)~Hammack and Goolsbee hawkish; December hike 91%; claims 200k vs 195k (medium, no score effect).|WEAKENED (scenario −1)~No new OAT–Bund reading since 142.4bp (10 Nov); euro-area GDP tomorrow 12:00 Bucharest.|CONFIRMED~UK Q3 GDP +0.7% q/q in line (Sept +0.2% vs 0.0%); not a clear beat. Dec BoE hike priced 66–73%.|INVALIDATED (toward stronger, carried); ~BoJ's Asada urged caution on the pace of hikes; Kihara: weak yen a problem. No fresh December pricing.|CONFIRMED~No new SNB item or Swiss data.|CONFIRMED~Brent $91.3, WTI $85.3 early Thursday; EIA figure not verified.|CONFIRMED~No verifiable RBA item or Australian release today.|CONFIRMED~No new item; dairy auction 17 Nov.|INVALIDATED by written rule (model still~Gold own score +7, or +4 if real yields keep rising; gold at its lowest since 4 Nov early Thursday.")
