    array.push(cH, "French bond stress crept back up just as the Fed's doves turned out to be hawks too.|The pound had a quiet night while the Fed's leadership circle added to the hawkish chorus.|The yen poked through 160 overnight, and Tokyo's warning lights are blinking again.|A wobble on Wall Street, a steady dollar, and a franc that still has nothing new to say.|Oil bounced hard on Middle East attacks, giving the loonie its first good headline in days.|The Aussie slipped toward its 2026 lows while the Fed kept turning the screw.|The kiwi's factories kept growing, just a little slower, while the Fed kept talking tough.|The French bond gap widened again, but not enough to break the tie with sterling.|Both of this pair's open questions moved toward the base case overnight.|The euro's escape route narrowed again, so the thin bearish lean is back on firmer ground.|French bond stress ticked higher, and the knife-edge pair leaned back toward its call.|A softer factory survey in New Zealand, a wider French spread, and still no winner.|Oil's sharp rebound gave Canada a lift, testing a lean that was already thin.|Quiet in London, loud around 160 in Tokyo.|No news for either side, and a small dose of Wall Street nerves in the background.|Two quiet currencies, and the Aussie keeps its slim lead on paper.|The kiwi's factories cooled a touch, but the tie with sterling holds.|Oil's bounce gave the loonie a breather, and this thin lean felt it.|The yen hit 160 against the dollar, and the bearish path for this pair didn't get closer.|Wall Street flinched a little, but not enough to pick a winner here.|The kiwi's factory survey cooled, nudging this thin lean the right way.|Oil bounced, and the commodity cousins' gap faces its first real test.|Kiwi factories cooled, and the yen sat right on Tokyo's red line.|A cooler kiwi factory survey and a jumpier Wall Street, both nudging the same way.|Oil's rebound gave Canada a lift, and this fragile lean got squeezed from both sides.|Oil jumped, the yen sank to 160: the lean holds, the extreme case still waits.|Oil rallied and markets got jumpier: a mixed night for this pair.|Two safe havens, one at Tokyo's red line, and still no clear winner.|Gold's three-day slide hit its lowest since October 2025, then bounced in Asia.")
